      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SLIP SLIDNAWAY (2) kicked off his career in good style last week, drawing on the back row and working forward to sit outside the leader before sticking on to be beaten 1.1 metres as runner-up at Penrith. Much better served by this barrier and is open to natural improvement. MAXIMIAN (1) showed good improvement when fourth here last start, beaten less than 2 metres. Fitter again third-up and should enjoy a nice run from the ace draw. POPS HOLLAQUIN (5) broke on debut but improved for third to a top filly at Menangle last time out. Could take another step forward. ULTIMATE CRUSADER (7) draws wide but deserves respect after winning two of his three starts here off a spell, one of them from this barrier.",
